# ─── Internal working notes — not part of the public source tree ───────────
# ANCHORED to the repo root on purpose. The unanchored form matched *any*
# directory named `internal/` at any depth — including `frontend/app/internal/`,
# a real Next.js route segment. That made the route invisible to git (so no
# review, hook, or CI diff ever saw it) while `next build` still compiled it
# from the working tree and served it. Keep the leading slash.
/internal/
/Internal/

# ─── FunctionPacks — public pack library (sources + bundled reference data) ───
!FunctionPacks/
!FunctionPacks/**
FunctionPacks/**/INTERNAL_NOTES.md
FunctionPacks/dist/
FunctionPacks/**/__pycache__/
FunctionPacks/**/*.pyc
FunctionPacks/**/*.egg-info/
FunctionPacks/**/.DS_Store
